-- title:
--   First mod p branch reads the level-one fibre field
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime, let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p` (a Deligne–Rapoport model package for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field of level $p$ over $\mathbb Z$, bundling properness, flatness, integrality and normality of `DRModel.toBase p`, rational and geometric curve models with their compatibilities, the two sections and the smooth locus), let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $K$ be a fraction field of $O$ and $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ a ring homomorphism. Write $X$ for the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z \to O$, assumed integral, and let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $X$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a perfect algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism, `data` a modular polynomial datum for $p$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr`, and $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ the integrality hypotheses on the two Hecke maps at level $1$; let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data at level $N=1$ and $R$ a prolongation tuple for $P$, with its two regular prolongations $R.R_1$, $R.R_2$ of $A$ inside `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`. Assume $\iota_K$ carries $O$ into $A$ and that $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ is the induced reduction, $\mathrm{to}\kappa(a) = \mathrm{red}(\iota_K(a))$. Let $\xi$ be the image under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` of the generic point of the curve of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k$, and consider the local ring of $X$ at $\xi$. Assume: (hφO) for every $a \in O$, $\varphi$ sends the germ at $\xi$ of the global function on $X$ determined by $a$ to the constant $\iota_K(a)$; (hval) $\varphi$ maps every germ at $\xi$ into the valuation subring $R.R_1.\mathrm{integers}$; (hloc) germs in the maximal ideal at $\xi$ have first residue `R.residue₁` equal to $0$; and (hj) some germ at $\xi$ is sent by $\varphi$ to `ProlongationTuple.jFun 1 p`, the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $j$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $\theta$ from $\operatorname{RatFunc} k$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the intermediate field of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`, which is the identity on the constants $k$ and which satisfies, for every germ $u$ at $\xi$: transporting $u$ along the stalk map of the branch at the generic point and then along the inverse of the function-field identification of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k$, and applying $\theta$, gives exactly `R.residue₁` of $\varphi(u)$.
--
--   In the Deligne–Rapoport picture the geometric fibre at $p$ of the model of $X_0(p)$ is two copies of the $j$-line crossing at the supersingular points; this statement identifies the function field of the first of the two labelled branches with the level-one fibre field $k(\tilde\jmath) =$ `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` over $k$, in a way compatible with the first residue of the prolongation tuple $R$ applied to $\varphi$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal), where the transported place of the branch point and the equality of orders are read off from $\theta$.
